{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1171253-the-song-of-achilles-in-cofd","id":1171253,"title":"The Song of Achilles in CofD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-28T10:00:36-08:00","id":1171253,"title":"The Song of Achilles in CofD","content":"As the title says, if one wanted to tell the story of <i>The Song of Achilles</i> (a really fantastic book which I heartily recommend to those who haven't read it) in the World of Darkness with the main characters (Achilles, Patroclus and Thetis in particular) as supernaturals, which kinds do you guys think would be best?<br /> <br /> Personally, I would cast Thetis as either a powerful Beast or Vampire and Achilles as a hero or a dhampir respectively. As for Patroclus, I would personally propose a Mage, likely Thyrsus or possibly Acanthus. That said, I could certainly see the whole triad as mages of various stripes. Perhaps Thetis is a politically and magically powerful Moros or maybe Mastigos of the Silver Ladder, and Achilles could definitely be interpreted as an Obrimos of the Adamantine Arrow. It would justify the names as well, with Shadow Names.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? This is just a thought that struck me out of the blue and I was wondering if anyone else would be willing to weigh in on the matter. It might be too off-topic for this section of the forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T10:32:29-08:00","id":1171262,"title":"","content":"We should yor your fansplat for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T10:53:41-08:00","id":1171266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1171253-the-song-of-achilles-in-cofd?p=1171262#post1171262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should yor your fansplat for it!</div> </div> </div> </div>What, Demigod? I could see it, but I'd prefer to keep to the canon splats, if you don't mind. The current version of Demigod is actually partially inspired by Madelaine Miller's representation of divinity and was kind of designed more-or-less for this kind of 'divinity deals with reality' story, so it'd be a bit too much like shooting fish in a barrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 12-28-2017, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T11:07:22-08:00","id":1171271,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it, it might be better to cast Patroclus as a Sleepwalker or a Proximus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T11:30:46-08:00","id":1171277,"title":"","content":"Okay,so Achilles? He's got all the marks of a deviant,he's got one superpower and one weakness connected to that power. He's deeply attached to his family especially Patroclus,and he is prone to unstoppable rages and is very stubborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T11:33:00-08:00","id":1171278,"title":"","content":"However,Achilles is also a Legend and changelings thrive on Legends. He could be a fairest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T11:49:25-08:00","id":1171284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1171253-the-song-of-achilles-in-cofd?p=1171277#post1171277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay,so Achilles? He's got all the marks of a deviant,he's got one superpower and one weakness connected to that power. He's deeply attached to his family especially Patroclus,and he is prone to unstoppable rages and is very stubborn.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does fit. Thetis could be a member of the conspiracy that creates him, or at least grants him his abilities. However, i know very little about Deviant beyond the absolute basics, so I'll have little to contribute in that direction. <br /> <br /> That said, I need to nip something in the bud: Patroclus is not family to Achilles. Full Stop. <br /> <br /> Sorry, I finally managed to persuade myself to watch <i>Troy</i> and it wasn't as bad as I thought it would be. It was worse. MUCH worse. A large part of why the relationship between Patroclus and Achilles is so meaningful is because they aren't family, Patroclus doesn't have divine blood and Achilles loves him anyway. Now, whether you buy into the homosexual relationship hinted at by Homer, common at the time and which is a central element of <i>TSoA </i>or not, that friendship is vital to the story. <br /> <br /> ... I just realised that my apology turned into a mini-rant. My apologies for my failed apology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T11:52:08-08:00","id":1171287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1171253-the-song-of-achilles-in-cofd?p=1171278#post1171278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However,Achilles is also a Legend and changelings thrive on Legends. He could be a fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would certainly fit with his looks, and <i>TSoA</i> Thetis would work surprisingly well as a Keeper, albeit a comparatively 'friendly' one. To Achilles. Only Achilles. And that motherly love motivates her to take him back with her so that he can be her 'perfect immortal amoral son' but meh, details. How would Patroclus fit into this story, though? Another Changeling? I still kinda like the idea of Patroclus as a neophyte mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 12-28-2017, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T11:59:31-08:00","id":1171291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1171253-the-song-of-achilles-in-cofd?p=1171284#post1171284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does fit. Thetis could be a member of the conspiracy that creates him, or at least grants him his abilities. However, i know very little about Deviant beyond the absolute basics, so I'll have little to contribute in that direction.<br /> <br /> That said, I need to nip something in the bud: Patroclus is not family to Achilles. Full Stop.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I finally managed to persuade myself to watch <i>Troy</i> and it wasn't as bad as I thought it would be. It was worse. MUCH worse. A large part of why the relationship between Patroclus and Achilles is so meaningful is because they aren't family, Patroclus doesn't have divine blood and Achilles loves him anyway. Now, whether you buy into the homosexual relationship hinted at by Homer, common at the time and which is a central element of <i>TSoA </i>or not, that friendship is vital to the story.<br /> <br /> ... I just realised that my apology turned into a mini-rant. My apologies for my failed apology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh i did not know that,I could swear remember reading somewhere they were cousins.<br /> and about deviant,just about everyone except the writers and the people who read the manuscript on a con know anything besides the basics. What we know is mostly that they have powers,that most of those powers have weaknesses too. That they form attachments to people to not become inhuman,and that almost all of them have a deep anger directed at their enemies.<br /> the bit about attachments helping them become more human seems fitting to Achilles,in a Deviant story,his love for Patroclus is what stops him to become a utterly inhuman warrior controlled by anger and anger alone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T12:03:27-08:00","id":1171293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1171253-the-song-of-achilles-in-cofd?p=1171287#post1171287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would certainly fit with his looks, and <i>TSoA</i> Thetis would work surprisingly well as a Keeper, albeit a comparatively 'friendly' one. To Achilles. And that motherly love motivates her to take him back with her so that he can be her 'perfect immortal amoral son' but meh, details. How would Patroclus fit into this story, though? Another Changeling? I still kinda like the idea of Patroclus as a neophyte mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages thrive on symbols,their magic based on ideas,I could see Patroclus using battle magic and that magic being strengthened by achile's armor as a symbol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T12:07:48-08:00","id":1171295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1171253-the-song-of-achilles-in-cofd?p=1171291#post1171291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh i did not know that,I could swear remember reading somewhere they were cousins.<br /> and about deviant,just about everyone except the writers and the people who read the manuscript on a con know anything besides the basics. What we know is mostly that they have powers,that most of those powers have weaknesses too. That they form attachments to people to not become inhuman,and that almost all of them have a deep anger directed at their enemies.<br /> the bit about attachments helping them become more human seems fitting to Achilles,in a Deviant story,his love for Patroclus is what stops him to become a utterly inhuman warrior controlled by anger and anger alone</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the only place where they're cousins is <i>Troy</i>. Anyway, details.<br /> <br /> Well, that does sound almost perfect for Achilles. The only bit that's missing is his hunger for glory, renown and a place in the memory of others and the age. The question is what thetis would be. Would she be an elder, inhuman Deviant who chose to work with the organization that 'augmented' her and her son? Simply a member of that organization? For that matter, would Achilles actually be her son or something else, a favoured project or similar? The style of 'augmentation' would probably be closer to the occult than to technology.<br /> <br /> Actually, that's an idea: What if the organization that made Achilles what he is is a sect of mages experimenting with mythic archetypes, and Achilles was originally a 'normal' person onto whom they'velaid the archetype of Achilles the hero; so that he's somewhere between the wielder of the power and a reincarnation of Achilles? In this story, Thetis is the Shadow Name of a powerful mage who runs or is heavily involved with the group and, as it mentions in <i>Mage</i> 2e her Shadow Name is an influence upon her. Patroclus could be either involved at a low level as a mage or Proximus, an outsider who stumbles across Achilles or the group or something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 12-28-2017, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T12:52:13-08:00","id":1171310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1171253-the-song-of-achilles-in-cofd?p=1171295#post1171295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, the only place where they're cousins is <i>Troy</i>. Anyway, details.<br /> <br /> Well, that does sound almost perfect for Achilles. The only bit that's missing is his hunger for glory, renown and a place in the memory of others and the age. The question is what thetis would be. Would she be an elder, inhuman Deviant who chose to work with the organization that 'augmented' her and her son? Simply a member of that organization? For that matter, would Achilles actually be her son or something else, a favoured project or similar? The style of 'augmentation' would probably be closer to the occult than to technology.<br /> <br /> Actually, that's an idea: What if the organization that made Achilles what he is is a sect of mages experimenting with mythic archetypes, and Achilles was originally a 'normal' person onto whom they'velaid the archetype of Achilles the hero; so that he's somewhere between the wielder of the power and a reincarnation of Achilles? In this story, Thetis is the Shadow Name of a powerful mage who runs or is heavily involved with the group and, as it mentions in <i>Mage</i> 2e her Shadow Name is an influence upon her. Patroclus could be either involved at a low level as a mage or Proximus, an outsider who stumbles across Achilles or the group or something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>i like it man,i'm SO freaking onboard with that idea, Mage and Deviant may be my favorite crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T12:59:59-08:00","id":1171312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1171253-the-song-of-achilles-in-cofd?p=1171310#post1171310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i like it man,i'm SO freaking onboard with that idea, Mage and Deviant may be my favorite crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do go together extremely well. If I was to write this, I'd probably have a period after the two meet during which Achilles is very distrustful of Patroclus on basis of him being a mage, with him slowly warming to him. Maybe have them encounter one another after Achilles escapes Pthyia (what I'm calling the 'organization' for the time being) and have Patroclus take the other in. It's a kind of reflection of the events of <i>TSoA</i>, wherein Patroclus is sent to live in the court of Achilels' father.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T13:01:38-08:00","id":1171314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1171253-the-song-of-achilles-i